From 8b903669599e492c904665c589e6e600feb6a411 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 02:49:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/34] WP24: Terms, DPA and manual-filing texts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Terms 1.6 (EN, CS), from compliance/04_terms_clauses.md with the owner's
decisions: § 5 stay fee duty; § 10 rewritten as 10.1 to 10.5 (filing on the
host's instruction, with the host's own access and in the host's name; filing
by hand, recorded with "I filed this stay by hand in UbyPort"); new § 10a
UbyPort access credentials ("zmocňuje" / "authorises and mandates"); § 13
best effort with notice of planned downtime where possible, no maintenance
window; § 17 cap of the fees paid in the 12 months before the claim and at
least CZK 10,000, never limited for intent or gross negligence (§ 2898
občanský zákoník).

DPA 1.6: § 11 lists Render and Google Drive only as "only if used" rows.

Terms, Privacy and DPA show one effective date, config.LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE
(UBYHOST_LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE), with the configured version, so all three
1.6 versions are accepted once on /account/accept.

Guide "If UbyHost cannot file in time" follows
compliance/05_manual_filing_fallback.md: when to file by hand, the UbyPort
web application URL and helpline, steps, keeping the Doručenka, then pressing
"I filed this stay by hand in UbyPort".

Integration: tests/test_legal_contents.py accepts the "10a" anchor;
tests/test_filing_watchdog.py compares escaped guide text.

Conflict resolution: privacy.html header: WP27's privacy-first line (earlier in this order) stays above the effective-date line, which now prints legal_effective('privacy').
